# Velocity by hand (0.15.23): on JAM, SEL held makes a key an accent (and not the shift); an Akai MPK mini (MIDI IN's Notes: MPK): its keys play the
# JAM page's voice with their velocity, its pads (channel 10) are the pads' bank A, its knobs (CC 24-31, steps; 70-77, places) the FX knobs, the
# acid, the bass and the mood. The pluck's MIDI out shows the velocity: 40 + 87 x the level (a plain key 0.95: 122, an accent 127).
seed 0
wait 3000
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
tap GLO
wait 100
spin SELECT 1
wait 100
spin SELECT 1
wait 200
expect view 33
expect jamv 0
key 5 down
wait 100
expect lastvel 122
key 5 up
wait 100
press SEL
wait 100
key 7 down
wait 100
expect lastvel 127
key 7 up
release SEL
wait 100
expect view 33
# the MPK on MIDI IN
press HOME
wait 900
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 7
wait 100
expect fxpage 26
spin K1 1
wait 100
spin K1 1
wait 100
spin K1 1
wait 200
expect minpads 3
shot midiin_mpk.png
# a key at velocity 64: the pluck at 0.95 x 0.64
midi 90 3C 40
wait 100
expect lastvel 92
midi 80 3C 00
# a key on the MPK (and a chord's notes let go with it)
tap PLAY
wait 300
# pad 9 (bank B's first, note 44 on channel 10): the breakdown on the bar
midi 99 2C 64
wait 2500
expect sec 1
# the knobs: the MK4's (CC 24-31) are endless and send steps (1 a click right, 127 a click left): the filter two right and one back, the eighth (the mood)
# two right; an older MPK's (CC 70-77) send places: its third (CC 72) full is Throw at 100
midi B0 18 01
midi B0 18 01
midi B0 18 7F
midi B0 1F 02
midi B0 48 7F
wait 100
expect fxk0 2
expect mood 54
expect fxk2 100
# kept
wait 6000
reboot
wait 3000
expect minpads 3
